WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:02.790
Instructor: So this next section is a big one

00:02.790 --> 00:05.160
in terms of the number of commands we cover.

00:05.160 --> 00:07.800
We talk about at least four,

00:07.800 --> 00:09.660
maybe five different commands.

00:09.660 --> 00:11.850
The thing that binds them all together is

00:11.850 --> 00:14.700
that they help you either undo changes

00:14.700 --> 00:18.822
or go back in time or view changes from earlier.

00:18.822 --> 00:21.090
But there's not just one thing we talk about.

00:21.090 --> 00:22.470
There's not just one command.

00:22.470 --> 00:23.820
So compared to other sections,

00:23.820 --> 00:25.980
at least other recent sections where you know

00:25.980 --> 00:28.110
it was like Git Merge for the whole section,

00:28.110 --> 00:31.350
or Git Branch the whole section, or Git Diff.

00:31.350 --> 00:34.558
This section is a Motley Crew of different commands.

00:34.558 --> 00:37.560
And a lot of them are good to know about for sure

00:37.560 --> 00:42.390
and and are useful at times, but they are not things you use

00:42.390 --> 00:45.810
on a daily basis unless you're like constantly messing up,

00:45.810 --> 00:48.390
and constantly needing to revert

00:48.390 --> 00:51.150
or reset your work and undo commits.

00:51.150 --> 00:54.300
Which personally doesn't happen to me like daily.

00:54.300 --> 00:58.110
Certainly I make mistakes or I want to undo changes,

00:58.110 --> 01:00.450
but not as much as I want to make commits,

01:00.450 --> 01:02.190
for example, or make branches.

01:02.190 --> 01:04.920
Anyway, we're gonna start by talking about checking

01:04.920 --> 01:07.800
out commits in something called Detached HEAD

01:07.800 --> 01:09.810
and how to get out of it or how to fix it.

01:09.810 --> 01:11.100
It's not really a problem,

01:11.100 --> 01:13.740
but recognizing what that means.

01:13.740 --> 01:16.260
And then we'll talk about discarding changes

01:16.260 --> 01:17.430
with Git Checkout.

01:17.430 --> 01:18.750
I'll say that's important.

01:18.750 --> 01:20.880
Git Restore is important.

01:20.880 --> 01:24.690
Git Resets, and Git Revert, Revert, Revert.

01:24.690 --> 01:25.680
Very confusing, right?

01:25.680 --> 01:27.180
Restore, reset and revert.

01:27.180 --> 01:28.740
They all kind of sound like they might do

01:28.740 --> 01:30.360
the exact same thing.

01:30.360 --> 01:31.890
So they're all gonna be marked,

01:31.890 --> 01:34.470
or I just marked them all as important,

01:34.470 --> 01:37.980
as I've mentioned when you need them, they are critical,

01:37.980 --> 01:40.020
but you may not need them all that much.

01:40.020 --> 01:42.690
I wanna refrain from putting everything ever in critical.

01:42.690 --> 01:45.490
I mean it's in this course because it's worth knowing,

01:45.490 --> 01:49.110
but these topics in particular, I'd say just don't come up

01:49.110 --> 01:51.240
as much as this stuff over here.

01:51.240 --> 01:53.580
So definitely don't skip this section,

01:53.580 --> 01:55.530
but because there are so many different commands

01:55.530 --> 01:57.870
I have a feeling it could be a little bit intimidating.

01:57.870 --> 01:59.880
So keep that in mind as you're learning them, right?

01:59.880 --> 02:01.530
You don't need to commit them to memory

02:01.530 --> 02:03.840
or you may not remember them as easily just

02:03.840 --> 02:05.370
because you don't use them as much.

02:05.370 --> 02:07.231
Okay, let's get started with all these similar

02:07.231 --> 02:08.080
sounding commands.

02:08.080 --> 02:09.033
Here we go.
